      "id": "PR_kwDOLyTYAM7NSTd2",
      "title": "protocol: drop overlapping span batches",
      "author": "sebastianst",
      "number": 371,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nDesign doc proposing a Karst hardfork derivation rule change: drop overlapping span batches instead of performing expensive `SafeBlockFetcher`-backed overlap verification.\n\n- **Derivation rule change** is straightforward — drop overlapping span batches post-Karst, remove `SafeBlockFetcher` from batch checking\n- **Fault proof interaction** is an open design question — nine approaches explored, none fully satisfactory. The most viable (deferred L2 block fetching) retains overlap complexity, raising the question of whether the rule change is worth the protocol cost\n- All approaches include concrete attack scenarios or limitations\n\nRelated: https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/pull/19303\n\n🤖 *Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)*",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/design-docs",
      "createdAt": "2026-03-25T09:45:21Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-04-02T11:38:39Z",
      "additions": 264,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLyTYAM7PbII8",
      "title": "feat: design doc for kona prestate native build",
      "author": "ajsutton",
      "number": 372,
      "body": "## Summary\n\n- Design doc for refactoring the kona prestate build to support both native (non-Docker) and reproducible Docker paths from a single definition\n- Extracts build logic from Dockerfile stages into `just` targets in `rust/justfile`\n- Reduces `cannon-builder` Docker image to apt packages only; tools installed via `mise` from shared `mise.toml`\n- Follows the proven pattern from `op-program/Dockerfile.repro` + `op-program/repro.justfile`\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] Review design doc for completeness and accuracy\n- [ ] Validate proposed architecture against current kona prestate build\n- [ ] Confirm CI impact analysis covers all affected jobs\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
